WEBVTT

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.710
We have two visitors.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.300
I'm coming.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.680
Why don't you sit down and paint normally for once?

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.190
I'm the one that has to clean it
and bow my head to the landlord.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.650
We finally have a garden, after all.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.660
Master Sori.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.540
Blade of the Immortal

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.960
One, two, three

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.250
Undead tree

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.670
What truth

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.340
I'll come true

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:45.520
Wow...

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.400
I see that bright light

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.780
This is all I have

00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:00.280
What did you say?
I know

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.830
Why do you say?

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.500
Hone the blade lie around

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:17.220
Survive of vision
Death and pleasure are my future

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.550
I got lost
I was lost

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.310
Survive of vision

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.600
Unfinished heaven

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.360
Now fight to claim your wounds

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:36.110
Don't know why
Don't know why

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:40.910
Survive of vision

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.590
Could it be, little Rin?

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:55.880
It's been a while.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.050
Sorry, I didn't notice you at first.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.840
So it was Rin!

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.350
Sir, you move around too much.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.720
-It took so long to find you--
-Hey!

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.810
This isn't time for some season's greetings.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.810
Who even is this guy?

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.980
He's just some local artist.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:17.860
We did all this searching because you said there was
some incredible swordsman who'd join us.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:22.990
You must've been abandoned by Mount Takao
at birth, then raised by some friendly monkeys.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.990
That's the vibe I'm getting from you.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:30.660
Sir! This... This man is my bodyguard.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.540
Bodyguard?

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.210
We'd known each other since childhood.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:43.260
Long ago, near Honjo, when I was studying
to become a mirror crafter,

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.300
I had a customer under the Asano family.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:51.190
I thought Asano was the kind of person
who would never incur resentment from others.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.100
To think he was killed by a grudge of the past.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.650
It's almost unbearable to imagine.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.480
I'm sorry.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.610
I thought I should've told you sooner...

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.610
but I was still sorting out my own emotions too.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.780
No, thank you.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.660
I'm glad you told me.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.660
I should be the one apologizing.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.460
I wasn't even at the funeral.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.750
It's all right, sir.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:17.670
Father's funeral
is only just now beginning.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.880
Revenge?

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.680
Father and Mother were innocent!

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:28.140
To that end, I've trained until I bled for two years.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.640
I even hired a bodyguard!

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:33.310
It's a fool's dream.
Please consider your own limitations.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.810
It's not a dream!

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:40.860
The rumors of that man, Anotsu, I've heard them too.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:47.780
The 22-year-old master swordsman, a self-purported
prodigy. Thanks to that forceful school being unified,

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:53.250
every dojo east of Katsushika has been destroyed.
The only survivors have become converts.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.960
Why does the shogunate allow it?

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.420
They may be worried that if there were a duel between
two master ronins,

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.470
and the government official made a wrong move,
there would be a great fuss about it.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:06.930
And there could also be some other dubious reasons.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:12.770
Either way, they're an outlaw gang that even
the shogunate doesn't want to mess with.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.560
Hiring a single bodyguard won't
give them any cause to worry.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.730
That may be the case.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:22.690
But there's still one path to make
the impossible possible, isn't there?

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.570
Like if I had just one more bodyguard.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.910
I can't offer that kind of assistance.

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.500
You haven't heard me out!

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.790
What are you asking of a mere painter?

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.170
I couldn't ask this of a mere painter.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:44.420
The master I'm asking is a spy of the shogunate.

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.220
I can't believe you knew that.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.600
That Asano, he was a troublesome man, too.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:58.270
The reason you were hired as a spy was because
they valued your connections and prowess with a sword.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:01.150
And I hear your swordplay surpasses even my father's.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.570
You see, if a painter

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.240
isn't always touching something new,

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.530
his sensibility immediately gets rusty.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:13.950
And for me, for example, Western paintings
and etchings.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:20.250
But as you know, if you were to collect those things
in this country right now, you'd be a criminal.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.000
So what should I do?

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.880
It would be best for me to remain
on the side of oversight.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.720
You mean staying a spy...

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.600
In order to gain the favor of the shogunate,
I polished my sword skill

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.180
and disposed of any anti-shogunate influence I had.
I even sold out fellow painters.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.390
My sword is mired in filth.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.310
I don't have a mind to wield it for a friend.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:49.320
Wow, thanks for that viewpoint. It was good for a laugh.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:53.870
Rin, the bottom of this guy's heart is lost.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.370
Tell me, old man.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:07:00.210
Between lending your dirty hand
to your old pal's kid when she needs it

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.540
and letting her die a painful death,

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:06.090
which one is sadder?

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:09.170
Be honest, mister.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:13.180
You can talk about dirtiness
and imply friendship all you want...

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:17.100
but in the end, you're just prioritizing
your own convenience.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.230
What really makes me laugh

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:25.270
is whatever disposition causes you to turn to sophistry
and muddy the waters when talk gets serious.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.570
A rather immature opinion, but I won't deny it.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.070
I've a mountain of paintings to finish.
You won't shame me for that.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.700
If you were an artist, you'd feel the same.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:38.910
Art, huh? You old bastard.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.250
-Hey, Mr. Manji! Where are you going?
-The discussion's over.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.130
I'm going to look for tonight's lodging.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.340
Paint to your heart's content, mister!

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.670
Wait!

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.470
The sun is setting. You can stay here.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:57.510
But...

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:01.480
We'll have lots to talk about in the morning.
Besides, you needn't worry.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:06.190
He's not the kind of man who would disappear
and abandon you.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.370
Rin. Rin?

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.120
Mother?

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:24.250
Rin.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.590
I'm still sleepy.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.090
Rin.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.720
You're such a sleepyhead.

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.180
Die!

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.100
Damn it!

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.730
You can move pretty well for someone who
just woke up.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.570
You swine.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:09:00.290
Well, it's good fun to catch a butterfly
as it tries to escape--

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.710
You couldn't just hold off for a while?

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:10.000
I wanted to relish the tongue lashing
and dramatic exit from yesterday.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:11.920
Mr. Manji!

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:14.720
Well, actually, I was just at the fire tower over--

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:15.800
Not that!

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:16.720
Behind you!

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.010
Okay, boys!

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:21.640
Whoever kills this guy

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.520
is the new boss!

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.480
I see.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.440
You see?
You think you have the luxury of being relaxed?

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:31.940
Do you really think you can cut us all down
with one sword--?

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:37.200
It's no good! Still the wrong color.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:41.660
Is this all my path of painting will amount to
until I take revenge for my friend?

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.250
-Okay, I get it, I'm sorry!
-Get back here!

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.170
Mr. Manji, back me up here!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.580
Red. Yes, red!

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:54.170
And what comes to mind is a red
that I should remember having seen countless times.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.630
For example, what? A flower? No, that's not it.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.050
A gem? No. A sunset?

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.390
No, that might be a stretch.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:05.980
But a red with a foundation
similar to a sunset...

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:09.350
-Too slow!
 -It's certainly easier said than done.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.310
Let's see.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.650
He's here again!

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:15.610
Please, God, let me have a demon of a revelation!

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:25.040
It's done!

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.160
That's right. This is it.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.750
The most basic red.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.380
Now that I know, all that's left--

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.340
Where'd that bastard go?

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.840
What a wonderful spot you're in.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.100
You're way too loud with every move you make.

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.980
That's why you're out of breath. Idiot.

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:55.570
What?

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:57.530
Damn it.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.360
You freaking amateur!

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:04.080
This one always works on idiots
that get too heated.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.330
Mr. Manji!

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:06.540
And now...

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.880
Where do we go from here, huh?

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:16.880
You killed every single one of my allies.

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:21.760
I'll have you repay me by severing both your hands
and feet!

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:32.940
Just tell me one thing.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.980
Who is this?

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.740
Any person who would trample on art

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.200
can die.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.500
I simply cannot fathom it.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:54.790
Why do you want to protect this girl so badly
that you'd take such a beating?

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.550
Do you want to be drunk on the act of
sacrificing yourself for others?

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:02.590
Long ago, my little sister was killed right in front of me,
and it was my fault.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:08.350
If this girl's face didn't resemble my sister's
so closely, I wouldn't be doing something so dumb.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:11.980
In the end, the two of us are two of a kind.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.980
I see, I get it now.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:15.150
I thought I told you.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:21.030
Little Rin, with 30 ryo, you could surely avoid
sleeping outdoors for two or three years.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:24.570
Perhaps we are two of a kind. All I'm worried about

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:29.790
is whether you even have the leeway to protect
the way of life of another person.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.250
Am I wrong?

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:33.580
Goodness...

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.670
You can't even be honest with yourself at the very end?

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.300
Well, aren't these peculiar.

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.850
We only have two days.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:50.060
Rest assured, the sign out there isn't just for show.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:51.270
So, whose are these?

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:54.230
-Your father's?
-Oh, it's not like that.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.060
I thought so.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:58.190
These aren't the tools of your everyday man.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:04.530
I started this job two years ago, and you don't
catch the scent of stolen goods like these often.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.070
These aren't from any common samurai.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:07.990
For example...

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:12.200
Forget it, that's not important.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.160
I won't ask for details.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:17.330
Swords are made for killing people, after all.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:18.920
I... I suppose that's true.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:29.850
So, lady, what do you say to 2 ryo
for the sharpening job?

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:32.310
If you don't have it now, I can wait a couple days.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.140
Hey!

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:38.980
Lady, looks like you know your swords.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:41.820
You're something else!
That right there is a secondhand.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.650
By its looks, I'd say it came from somewhere in Yezo.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:49.200
Its owner should be back to pick it up soon.
He's from that school you hear about all the time.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:50.910
You probably know of it.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:53.290
I think it was the Itto-ryu...

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:54.410
Speak of the devil.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.540
Girl, what are you doing?

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:04.760
Now, now. This lady just seems to like swords.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:07.840
I was just going over her man's swords over there.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.010
Is that so? Pardon me.

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:17.440
You have my thanks.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:21.940
It being secondhand aside,
this one's ease of use is in a league of its own.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.150
It's not fit for the hands of an amateur.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:29.490
Oh, boy, if I sharpened something like that,
it'll give me the chills.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:33.620
The kind of therapeutic chills that feel
like a nice, cool evening breeze.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.540
It's an impressive life you live.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.040
I'll stop by again someday.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.870
Sure, I appreciate it.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.080
Hey!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.040
Mr. Samurai!

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.460
Please hand over that sword to me!

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:48.800
I can furnish you with up to 30 ryo.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:50.760
I beseech you, please.

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:55.970
I'm no samurai. Just a swordsman.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:15:01.810
Girl, do you know of the Asano dojo that was in
Honjo up until two years ago?

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:03.980
Yes.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:07.240
I'm searching for a girl from that dojo.

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.860
I can't sell this sword for any amount of money.

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:15.240
If you were to tell me where this girl is,

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:18.040
I would consider your request.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:20.040
How about it?

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.960
It's fine with me. I'm used to it.

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:30.470
But for you to just suddenly go broke...

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:33.260
Can you go without a bath or food?

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.180
I'm sorry.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:40.440
Why do you want someone else's sword so badly?

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.190
It was my father's.

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:49.110
Two years ago, every single sword in the dojo
was stolen.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.660
It was among those.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.870
So, what do you want to do?

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:58.120
Did you catch where they were staying?

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.750
Will you take it back by force?

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:04.830
They said they'll be at an inn called Takiguchi
nearby Jimon until tomorrow.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:05.960
But...

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.550
I'm sorry, Mr. Manji.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:15.180
This is the last time I'll bring up stuff like this.

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:17.470
I'm already 16.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:21.600
It's disgraceful for me to always be
prattling on about Father and Mother.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:24.600
I've already moved past this sword business.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:28.820
That guy's a swordsman of the Itto-ryu, too.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.360
Don't you despise him?

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:34.530
I do. I hate him...

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.830
but as long as Kagehisa Anotsu lives,
my enemies will only grow in number.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.540
I won't take unnecessary steps.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.750
I need to take
the shortest route to that man.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:03.770
Your face, I've seen it on a wanted poster.

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:07.690
You're a former armed constable.
I believe the charges were

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.230
the killing of 100 men.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:14.700
I don't know what you want with me,
but I hope it doesn't take too long.

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:19.160
Oh, it's not that big a deal.
There's just a bit of a situation.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:21.120
Fight me.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.370
In the event that I win,

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:27.500
I'll have the longer sword that's on your waist.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:33.130
Hilarious! I see. So that's how it is?

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:37.390
So that girl back then really was the one
I was looking for. Well?

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:44.140
Isn't that right, Mr. Manji? So the one who killed
Sabato Kuroi and Nisaburo Tsuchimochi was you.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.640
Tsuchimo? The bald guy with the--?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:48.100
The bald guy with the spear.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:57.070
Get back here!

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:06.540
You little--

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.460
I like this guy.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:18.430
That's right. It had to come to this.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:22.140
Give me your name! I'll make sure I remember it!

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:26.600
Magatsu. Taito Magatsu.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:31.730
You're the first person other than my allies
who hasn't died after this many moves.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.780
That said, I've drawn first blood.

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:35.690
This, huh?

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:38.150
Well, you did surprise me.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.700
Sorry, but I'm used to this level of adversity.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:47.540
Now there's some nostalgia.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.830
I was born in the village of Senzoku.

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:53.420
The house I was born in is just a stone's throw from here.

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:58.420
This entire area was hit by a flood.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:03.680
And despite the shape this forest is in, it was
able to absorb the water and fuse in the mud.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:10.650
One of my childhood friends, seemingly unaware of this,
died in the mud, later to be found by me.

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:14.770
The place I found him happens to be exactly
where you're standing!

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:16.280
What?

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:33.590
For whatever reason, I'm remembering the past.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:35.710
I had a younger sister.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:41.430
Mari was kicked by the Daimyo's horse,
and was torn in two.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:46.760
Mr. Manji, if you were a samurai in the past,
then you're my enemy.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:48.680
The girl that was with you, as well.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:52.690
There isn't a samurai family alive that's without sin.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.940
They live their lives, guaranteed to harm others.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.830
You're not the only

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:10.080
lone, tragic hero, you know.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:18.170
I won't let you kill me ever again.

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:28.060
You think a wound like this is enough?
A wound like this?

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:32.730
This was quite the riveting night, Mr. Manji.

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:38.400
I hope someday we'll get to enjoy
a night like this together again.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:42.650
Assuming we both survive this one, that is.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:47.830
Ouch.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:50.330
Mr. Manji!

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:52.790
This was here when I woke up.

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:56.750
Oh, what the heck? So you ended up
spending that 30 ryo?

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.710
Don't play dumb!

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:02.670
Who the hell asked you to do that?
I told you I was over it.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:08.390
If you suffer pain for my selfishness, or even die--

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:09.600
I won't die.

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:12.060
Idiot! Damn it!

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.180
Then should I toss it?

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:16.520
Rin, what's with you?

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:21.190
You resolved to take this journey due to the pain
of having your parents killed.

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:25.950
If you become unable to shed a single tear
for your parents,

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:29.280
would you even be able to keep journeying?

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:31.700
Even if they're all painful memories,

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:36.290
if you can remember them, there will be times
you can summon up unbelievable strength.

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:40.000
I guess I won this time.

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.720
Big bro, you idiot.

00:21:45.590 --> 00:21:46.800
What did you just say?

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:48.430
Weren't you listening?

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:49.800
I'm not going to say it again.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:53.980
I look like her, don't I?
Your little sister.

00:21:54.060 --> 00:21:56.980
It's not fair if I'm the only one who cries.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:00.150
You need to let me see you cry now and then.

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:02.820
You dumbass, why the hell would I cry?

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:07.530
Quit spouting weird stuff and close the door already.
Don't bother me till noon.

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:09.410
Sorry.

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:13.120
Besides, the way you call me is different.
You've got it wrong.

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:15.620
It's not "big bro."

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:16.960
It's "big brother."

00:22:18.620 --> 00:22:20.040
Big brother, you idiot!

00:23:49.300 --> 00:23:52.300
Act Two – Founding
